# Remittance API assignment

Help the user build a hiring pre-assignment: Korea -> Philippines remittance REST API.

## Scope

Current work is PART 2 (optional). Part 1 is done and working. Never change Part 1 S1–S6 results.

Change only what the user asked in this step. Do not build ahead.

## Stack

Java 17, Spring Boot 3, Spring Data JPA, H2 in-memory, Maven.

## Schema

- Root `schema.sql` is the only schema source.
- Hibernate `ddl-auto` must be `none`.
- Spring loads it with `spring.sql.init.schema-locations=file:./schema.sql`.

## Money

- Code: `BigDecimal`. DB: `BIGINT` (KRW), `DECIMAL(19,2)` (PHP). API: JSON strings.
- Never use `double` or `float`.

## Errors

Every non-2xx body is exactly `{"error": "<CODE>", "message": "<text>"}`.

- `VALIDATION_ERROR` (400), `NOT_FOUND` (404), `CONFLICT` (409)
- Part 2 adds only `LIMIT_EXCEEDED` (422), same shape

Do not build a custom error framework.

## Do not add

Auth, list queries, pagination, Docker, CI, Swagger, metrics, health checks.

## Style

Keep code simple. The user must explain every line in an interview. Comments and docs are short, easy English.

## Part 2

- A successful partner call is acceptance only. Only callback handling sets `COMPLETED`.
- Do not hold a DB transaction or lock during the partner call.
- Status changes are conditional updates: `WHERE status = expected status`.
- No randomness. Partner failures are deterministic.
- Code that needs time takes an injected `java.time.Clock`.
